:author Laluxx
:version 0.1.0
:keywords obsidian tests contract stable-identity-contract

;;; Commentary:

stable-identity-contract.mon — live engine identity test fixtures (Cycle 23).
Run inside a real embedded Monad engine; requires an initialized scene.
These are deliberately NOT counted as executed by headless `make test`.
Interactive procedure:
1. (define saved (node 0))
2. Add unrelated nodes in the editor.
3. (node-name saved) succeeds, (node-index saved) returns the new slot.
4. Delete the saved node -> (node-name saved) must reject a stale handle.
5. Repeat with (mesh 0), using an unrelated mesh add/delete/reallocation.
6. Reset the scene -> both kinds of previously held handles expire.

;;; Code:
(define (obsidian-test-stable-node-roundtrip)
  (let ([saved (node 0)])
    (= (node-name saved)
       (node-name (node (node-index saved))))))

(define (obsidian-test-stable-mesh-roundtrip)
  (let ([saved (mesh 0)])
    (= (mesh-name saved)
       (mesh-name (mesh (mesh-index saved))))))
